content:
{
  "summary": "This scan found four items, all about the user accounts on this computer. The most important is that the Guest account is turned on and needs no password, which lets anyone sit down and sign in; look at that first. The built-in Administrator account is also on, and two extra administrator accounts are listed for you to confirm you recognize them. No earlier scan was available to compare against.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "priority": 1,
      "title": "Guest account is on with no password",
      "finding_ids": [
        "ACCT-GUEST-ENABLED:6684b413"
      ],
      "explanation": "The built-in Guest account is enabled and does not require a password. That means anyone with access to this computer can sign in without having an account of their own. Most personal computers don't need this turned on. The report shows how to address it for this finding."
    },
    {
      "priority": 2,
      "title": "Built-in Administrator account is on",
      "finding_ids": [
        "ACCT-BUILTIN-ADMIN-ENABLED:1b4c5dc7"
      ],
      "explanation": "Windows has a built-in account called Administrator, and here it is turned on. It does require a password, which is good, but because every Windows computer has this account with the same name, attackers know to try guessing its password. If you don't actively use it, the fix shown in the report is worth reviewing."
    },
    {
      "priority": 3,
      "title": "Confirm you recognize these administrator accounts",
      "finding_ids": [
        "ACCT-EXTRA-ADMIN:fde0b291",
        "ACCT-EXTRA-ADMIN:3df7405c"
      ],
      "explanation": "Two local accounts, <computer>\\<account-2> and <computer>\\<account-3>, have full administrator rights, meaning they can change anything on the computer. Having a separate admin account is often normal and even good practice, so these are rated low. Just check that you know who each one belongs to; an admin account you don't recognize would be a reason for concern. Since there was no earlier scan to compare with, the scan can't tell whether these were added recently."
    }
  ],
  "severity_notes": []
}
